; ======== KWP_SID21_ResolveLID_Descriptor  (@0xe3220) ========
        ; KWP SID 0x21 ReadDataByLocalIdentifier - per-LID descriptor resolver.
        ; Input: param_1 = LID byte. For each supported LID it commits:
        ;   DAT_00f93a = base of a LE16 RAM-pointer table (word const, e.g. LID 0x01 -> table @0xa1c08)
        ;   DAT_00f560 = entry count (byte const, e.g. LID 0x01 -> 0x24/36 @0xa2100)
        ; For LID 0x01 it also assembles ~13 composite status/flag bytes from dozens of live
        ; variables into the RAM staging block 0xf520..0xf52c, which the pointer table then
        ; references. Consumer: SID21 reader @0df638 loops count times doing resp[i]=*(byte*)table[i].
